   "id": "unit:bins-a",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "So airport security wants my belt in a bin. The bin gets my belt, my shoes and most of my confidence. I walk through the scanner holding my pants up like a man surrendering to his own laundry.",
   "date": "2024-03-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "unit:bins-b",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "The bin gets my belt, my shoes and my dignity. Airports are a spa where strangers touch you without asking.",
   "date": "2023-11-12"
  },
  {
   "id": "unit:parrot-a",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "I bought a parrot that only says legal disclaimers. Past results are no guarantee of future crackers. He read me my rights when I touched his perch.",
   "date": "2024-01-05"
  },
  {
   "id": "unit:landlord-a",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "My landlord started a group chat for the building. Every message is a threat with a thumbs up. He reacted to my rent with the crying laughing face.",
   "date": "2024-05-20"
  },
  {
   "id": "unit:laundry-a",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "The laundromat is the only place I meet women. We stare at our socks spinning like it is a fireplace. Nothing says romance like a dryer sheet stuck to my back.",
   "date": "2023-08-14"
  },
  {
   "id": "unit:gym-a",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "At the gym I stare at the mirror the way my parrot does. Mostly to check if anyone saw me drop the small weights.",
   "date": "2024-06-02"
  },
  {
   "id": "unit:gym-orphan",
   "type": "unit",
   "text": "Short.",
   "date": "2024-06-03"
  },
  {
